/*Well, good as I expected. If you enjoyed original Talisman and you love Warhammer, you'll enjoy this.*/
UPD: Well, it's November 2016 now, and I can say, that balance is still bad. Just look at Magnus, my god, every turn he can cast a spell and that spell WILL do something good for him.
AI is pretty stupid and you, actually, play against random cards, not the AI. It live in another dimension and you clash with AI twice per game. So, if you are fan of WH40K, you can enjoy this game, but if you enjoyed Talisman very much, don't expect T:THH to be that good.

Graphic concepts are very good and the gameplay itself is quite lovely. Still, there are major flaws that ruin the atmosphere.
Minuses:
- Presence of some "mandatory routes" that make the "open world" of the roofs look like invisible labirinth at times;
- At least once per chapter you are stuck and don't know where to go or what to do: often it is combined with combat, leaving little to no time to look at your surroundings;
- The routes are sometimes misleading, or require perfect (Perfect) timing to be run. Minimal errors often result to death and restart from the same point, which is frustrating;
- The plot is quite dull and gives little-to-no additional value to the game.
Pluses:
+ The idea of hidden bags, with marks to signal them;
+ The graphics are quite original, I personally like very much the idea of white + strong colors;
+ Unlimited sosias of Neo from Matrix disguised as police officers.

